{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2861af9a73966356710244eddb70a4f66935eca474db9f6aff03cfaf8fe6acc5","digest":{"component_or_area":"opcert service app worker lifecycle","key_entities":["src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py","test_matching_guard_is_accepted","test_worker_cancellation_survives_job_completion_race","test_worker_records_job_timeout","_worker","asyncio.wait_for","asyncio.timeout","asyncio.to_thread","lifespan","queue.get","cancelling()"],"problem_keywords":["python 3.11","asyncio.wait_for","cancellation race","xdist worker crash","lifespan teardown","CPython issue 86296"],"propositions":["Python 3.11 asyncio.wait_for consumes external worker cancellation when child future completes in same turn, causing worker to return to queue.get() with pending cancellation count while lifespan awaits forever.","TestClient teardown hangs for 300+ seconds on Python 3.11 after test_matching_guard_is_accepted when job completion collides with shutdown cancellation, whereas Python 3.12/3.13 pass.","Replacing asyncio.wait_for with Python 3.12-style asyncio.timeout semantics around asyncio.to_thread preserves external cancellation and per-job timeout while preventing race condition.","Regression oracle test_worker_cancellation_survives_job_completion_race is RED before fix and GREEN after on Python 3.11, and mutation restoring wait_for returns it to RED."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787525682041696001,"uuid":"cec31d21-9735-4e26-bb08-6e90d7810815"}